WEBVTT

00:07.610 --> 00:12.070
Les Misérables

00:07.610 --> 00:12.070
A Girl Named Cosette

00:08.610 --> 00:11.610
Beyond the wind

00:12.070 --> 00:15.490
The wind blows

00:12.070 --> 00:15.490
Kaze ga fuki nuketeku

00:15.490 --> 00:22.080
over the daisies blooming over the stone pavement

00:15.490 --> 00:22.080
Ishidatami ni saku hinagiku

00:22.080 --> 00:25.620
I held my knees

00:22.080 --> 00:25.620
Hiza wo tsuite

00:25.620 --> 00:31.090
and gazed at the flowers

00:25.620 --> 00:31.090
Jitto mitsumeteta

00:31.090 --> 00:34.840
Far away, very far away

00:31.090 --> 00:34.840
Tooku haruka tooku

00:34.840 --> 00:41.470
A gentle voice is calling me

00:34.840 --> 00:41.470
Watashi wo yobu yasashii koe

00:41.470 --> 00:45.060
Let's go look for it

00:41.470 --> 00:45.060
Sagashii ni yukou

00:45.060 --> 00:50.820
Even if we wander aimlessly

00:45.060 --> 00:50.820
Attemonai keredo

00:50.820 --> 00:55.570
The rain comes down

00:50.820 --> 00:55.570
Doushaburi no ame

00:55.570 --> 01:00.330
on a lonely morning

00:55.570 --> 01:00.330
Hitoribocchi no asa

01:00.330 --> 01:04.870
But look, beyond the clouds

01:00.330 --> 01:04.870
Demo hora kumo no mukou

01:04.870 --> 01:09.460
the sunlight is peering at us

01:04.870 --> 01:09.460
Hizashi ga nozoiteruyo

01:09.460 --> 01:11.840
Wipe away your tears

01:09.460 --> 01:11.840
Namida fuite

01:11.840 --> 01:14.760
Look forward

01:11.840 --> 01:14.760
Mae wo muite

01:14.760 --> 01:19.050
and summon all of your strength

01:14.760 --> 01:19.050
Ashimoto chikara komete

01:19.050 --> 01:21.390
Let's walk

01:19.050 --> 01:21.390
Aruite yukou

01:21.390 --> 01:23.770
I'm sure we will make it

01:21.390 --> 01:23.770
Kitto yukeru

01:23.770 --> 01:31.190
The road, the road, continues on...

01:23.770 --> 01:31.190
Michi wa michi wa tsuzuku yo...

01:31.190 --> 01:34.240
forever...

01:31.190 --> 01:34.240
Dokomademo

01:49.790 --> 01:54.590
Javert's Suspicions

02:03.320 --> 02:04.090
Monsieur Madeleine!

02:05.860 --> 02:07.720
Monsieur Madeleine! There's trouble!

02:20.290 --> 02:22.060
Save me...

02:23.210 --> 02:25.020
Someone has to bring the jack here.

02:25.210 --> 02:27.030
There should be one coming soon.

02:27.050 --> 02:28.070
No, it's not going to work.

02:28.470 --> 02:30.570
We've to save him right away.

02:31.850 --> 02:32.990
Mayor.

02:43.860 --> 02:45.590
Someone lend me a hand!

02:46.280 --> 02:48.260
Even if we lend a hand...

02:48.280 --> 02:49.800
It won't work, Mayor.

02:49.820 --> 02:51.900
If we mess up, we'd get crushed underneath.

02:52.620 --> 02:54.640
They're right.

02:54.660 --> 02:58.270
Human strength alone will not able to lift the wagon up.

02:59.160 --> 03:01.060
There isn't a human who can replace a jack...

03:02.580 --> 03:05.330
<i>No... One person could...</i>

03:09.010 --> 03:10.710
That prisoner could do it...

03:13.010 --> 03:16.160
That prisoner in Toulon could do it...

03:16.810 --> 03:18.120
Jean Valjean.

03:20.520 --> 03:24.080
Jean Valjean had attempted to escape from jail many times.

03:24.520 --> 03:28.590
He even stole a young lad's silver coin after being released from jail.

03:29.400 --> 03:33.430
He's a repeat offender, so he will not be able to
avoid life imprisonment when he gets arrested.

03:34.870 --> 03:41.560
If that man were here, then it might be possible to lift this wagon.

03:42.960 --> 03:45.310
Save me...

03:51.630 --> 03:55.950
People who can take the place of a jack don't
necessarily have to be that prisoner.

04:01.730 --> 04:02.500
Monsieur Madeleine!

04:20.910 --> 04:22.520
Pull him out now! Hurry!

04:24.420 --> 04:24.940
All right...

04:25.000 --> 04:25.900
He's been pulled out!

04:26.080 --> 04:27.900
Okay. Everyone, get away.

04:34.340 --> 04:35.420
As expected of the Mayor!

04:56.320 --> 04:58.010
His life is not in danger.

04:59.950 --> 05:03.020
But the joints of his knees are injured.

05:04.160 --> 05:09.020
Even after he recovers, it'd be difficult for him to carry heavy loads.

05:09.840 --> 05:11.690
He can't work on a wagon again.

05:18.090 --> 05:18.990
Mayor...

05:20.640 --> 05:21.580
I'm glad you're all right.

05:23.480 --> 05:25.960
I'm really down on my luck.

05:26.770 --> 05:31.920
I wonder how I am going to earn money with these legs of mine...

05:32.780 --> 05:34.840
You've pushed yourself hard up until now,

05:35.490 --> 05:39.430
so you should do some less exhaustive work from now on.

05:39.990 --> 05:43.140
Easier said than done. Where can I find such a job?!

05:43.160 --> 05:46.270
If it's so easily available, then no one would have to toil sweat and blood.

05:47.080 --> 05:52.610
You're right... Then I'll help you find one before
you are discharged from the hospital.

05:55.010 --> 05:59.410
In addition, you don't have to worry about your wagon and your horse.

06:00.600 --> 06:02.280
I'll buy them.

06:08.140 --> 06:11.790
Why are you doing so much for me?

06:12.610 --> 06:15.800
There isn't a need for a reason to help others.

06:18.860 --> 06:24.100
Please forgive me, Monsieur Madeleine. I feel ashamed of myself...

06:24.790 --> 06:27.560
You're a real Messiah.

06:27.830 --> 06:29.980
How can I repay this kindness...

06:30.580 --> 06:32.120
You don't have to repay me.

06:32.880 --> 06:39.400
You just have to treasure this feeling and pass
it on to others someday when they need help.

06:58.990 --> 07:01.050
Monsieur Madeleine is really amazing.

07:01.780 --> 07:05.600
The wagon was busted and the horse was dead too.

07:06.620 --> 07:11.640
Yet he isn't daunted by that and bought the
horse and the wagon wholeheartedly.

07:12.380 --> 07:16.020
Big brother, you have said that three times since you came back home.

07:17.090 --> 07:18.070
Is that so?

07:18.510 --> 07:24.030
But you want to say that Monsieur Madeleine
is really a marvelous person to the end, right?

07:24.640 --> 07:26.330
Yup, that's what I was saying!

07:27.060 --> 07:29.370
Now, let us all clear the table once we're done with dinner.

07:29.890 --> 07:31.540
I'll go and fetch water.

07:31.770 --> 07:33.790
Can I have another serving?

07:38.280 --> 07:39.420
What's wrong, Daniel?

07:42.160 --> 07:44.590
Inspector Javert? What's the matter?

07:45.160 --> 07:48.890
I want to ask something about Monsieur Madeleine.

07:49.500 --> 07:50.560
What do you want to ask?

07:51.960 --> 07:53.190
Go back inside.

07:54.420 --> 07:57.860
When did you start working for the Mayor?

07:58.460 --> 08:00.070
About 4 years ago.

08:00.880 --> 08:06.700
Do you know where Mayor Madeleine came
from before he arrived in this town?

08:07.220 --> 08:08.870
Well... I don't know.

08:10.140 --> 08:11.950
Why did you ask me these questions?

08:13.020 --> 08:14.790
It's nothing. I just wanted to know.

08:23.200 --> 08:26.340
Alain, can you deliver this to Monsieur Fauchelevent?

08:29.080 --> 08:33.600
It's a recommendation letter. I have found him
a job in a convent in Paris as a gardener.

08:34.670 --> 08:38.730
Speaking of which, Inspector Javert came all the way to my house last night.

08:38.750 --> 08:40.730
He asked things concerning you...

08:44.880 --> 08:45.860
Concerning me?

08:46.640 --> 08:51.740
He asked me if I knew where you came from before you arrived in this town.

08:53.980 --> 08:59.210
I'm sure that inspector finds it strange that you re such a capable person.

08:59.650 --> 09:04.720
Or that he wants to you help him to find a new job?

09:06.660 --> 09:08.300
So, I better get going then.

09:15.330 --> 09:18.650
The prisoner in Toulon could do it...

09:18.880 --> 09:20.480
Jean Valjean.

09:21.130 --> 09:27.570
If that man were here, then it might be possible to lift this wagon.

09:37.600 --> 09:40.130
Could he have noticed?

10:02.750 --> 10:05.230
Living expenses are to be raised to 10 francs next month.

10:06.260 --> 10:10.950
But I suppose that can't be helped. Cosette is turning eight soon.

10:10.970 --> 10:15.200
There are schooling and many other expenses.

10:16.140 --> 10:18.710
I ought to work harder.

10:19.810 --> 10:21.670
Mademoiselle Fantine!

10:22.520 --> 10:23.630
Are you reading a letter?

10:23.650 --> 10:25.000
No...

10:25.610 --> 10:28.170
You don't have to hide it like that.

10:28.200 --> 10:32.850
I'm sorry. But this letter is really important to me.

10:34.410 --> 10:36.560
I'm sure that the letter is sent by a man.

10:37.410 --> 10:41.400
Well, she's such a beauty. Therefore, men can't ignore her.

10:41.960 --> 10:46.570
The men in the factory are not attractive at all, so she doesn't talk to them.

10:47.470 --> 10:51.740
But she has gone to the post office many times to post letters.

10:52.180 --> 10:54.660
It must be a passionate love.

10:54.680 --> 10:59.220
If the other person was working in this factory,
she wouldn't have to go and send letters.

10:59.770 --> 11:02.170
I'm sure he's someone not in this town.

11:02.980 --> 11:04.420
Then who on earth could...

11:05.020 --> 11:06.880
He's not just a lover.

11:07.570 --> 11:10.340
Besides, she has sent quite a bit of money to him.

11:11.320 --> 11:13.590
They must have a secret that can't be told to anyone.

11:14.410 --> 11:15.260
A secret?

11:20.210 --> 11:21.140
A letter?

11:21.170 --> 11:23.690
No, this is just the envelope. It's empty inside.

11:24.000 --> 11:25.110
Where was it sent from?

11:26.210 --> 11:29.740
Montfermeil - Waterloo Inn.

11:49.320 --> 11:51.230
All right, I'm done with all of the chores.

11:51.610 --> 11:56.550
Cosette, are you going over to the priest again to learn to read today?

11:57.040 --> 11:57.510
Yeah.

12:12.970 --> 12:15.740
I have finished washing the clothes and the floor.

12:15.930 --> 12:17.160
Oh, is that so?

12:22.230 --> 12:25.000
I knew it. We're just barely making ends meet this month too.

12:25.270 --> 12:31.510
You don't have to worry at all. Living expenses
have been raised to 10 francs from next month.

12:31.860 --> 12:35.050
Will that woman really send the money over?

12:35.740 --> 12:39.970
Don't worry. The economy in Montreuil-sur-Mer is booming.

12:41.040 --> 12:43.020
Montreuil-sur-Mer?

12:45.380 --> 12:47.690
Excuse me. Sorry to intrude.

12:49.250 --> 12:50.520
Welcome!

12:51.340 --> 12:52.690
Cosette!

12:52.720 --> 12:56.950
Why are you idling there? If you're done with
the cleaning, go and do the shopping.

12:57.350 --> 12:59.490
Eh? I just went to do the shopping...

12:59.970 --> 13:06.330
Go again. We're getting a lot of people staying
today, so we don't have enough ingredients.

13:06.900 --> 13:09.500
Oh, please wait. I'll prepare the rooms right away.

13:21.490 --> 13:22.930
I suppose I can't go today.

13:26.290 --> 13:30.860
Cosette, go and learn to read. Chou Chou and I will do your shopping.

13:31.300 --> 13:32.900
You can't do that.

13:33.260 --> 13:35.690
It's fine. Right, Chou Chou?

13:39.140 --> 13:40.370
Let's go, Chou Chou.

13:48.560 --> 13:50.210
Toron!

13:53.530 --> 13:56.050
Say, how about coming to my house and play?

13:56.490 --> 13:59.050
The cakes that my mother bakes are really delicious.

13:59.740 --> 14:02.510
I'm sorry, but I have something to do today.

14:03.330 --> 14:04.220
Something to do?

14:04.250 --> 14:05.640
Yeah. I better get going.

14:21.100 --> 14:24.120
This is how you write "Montreuil-sur-Mer".

14:24.770 --> 14:25.830
Do you want to try and write?

14:25.890 --> 14:26.450
Yes.

14:28.980 --> 14:34.000
Montreuil-sur Mer.

14:34.780 --> 14:36.460
Priest. Cosette.

14:37.070 --> 14:38.170
What are you writing?

14:39.280 --> 14:41.300
We're writing Montreuil sur-Mer.

14:41.870 --> 14:44.470
It's the name of the town where my mother lives.

14:46.200 --> 14:50.520
If you learn how to write more words, you will
be able to write a letter to your mother.

14:51.210 --> 14:53.980
Write a letter to Mother?!

15:17.940 --> 15:20.220
Take this, Cosette, and bring it out to them.

15:20.820 --> 15:21.440
Yes.

15:25.120 --> 15:28.890
Oh yeah, what happened to Éponine today? I haven't seen her yet.

15:29.410 --> 15:33.150
She cooped herself up in her room after she got back from school.

15:33.840 --> 15:35.400
Did something happen?

15:36.460 --> 15:39.110
Azelma, do you have any idea?

15:39.380 --> 15:40.280
I don't know.

15:40.800 --> 15:43.860
I was playing with my doll all this time.

16:02.030 --> 16:05.140
You passed through Montreuil-sur-Mer?

16:05.450 --> 16:07.470
Its economy is pretty stable.

16:07.830 --> 16:10.270
Yes! Its black glass is really popular.

16:10.290 --> 16:11.810
Oh, this is the glass.

16:12.830 --> 16:15.560
I bought this black glass button as a souvenir.

16:16.750 --> 16:18.770
It really is a fashionable button.

16:18.800 --> 16:20.320
Is it a present for your lover?

16:20.340 --> 16:21.230
No, of course not.

16:21.510 --> 16:22.240
Do you want to have a look?

16:27.970 --> 16:28.870
Beautiful...

16:29.680 --> 16:33.580
So this is made in Montreuil-sur-Mer.

16:37.150 --> 16:38.750
<i>The city where Mother is in...</i>

16:39.030 --> 16:39.710
Hey!

16:41.320 --> 16:44.550
Cosette, you can't bother the customers.

16:44.910 --> 16:46.050
Y-Yes.

16:46.070 --> 16:49.220
Cosette, bring another bottle of wine over.

16:49.240 --> 16:49.820
Yes!

16:50.370 --> 16:52.220
I'll carry them.

16:52.250 --> 16:54.480
No, please sit down.

16:54.500 --> 16:57.980
Our inn has a really fantastic story.

17:00.300 --> 17:03.030
Here, young man. Drink more.

17:04.340 --> 17:06.860
Listen well to what I have to say.

17:07.430 --> 17:11.490
I will tell you why our inn is called the Waterloo Inn.

17:13.810 --> 17:17.960
It happened back in the Battle of the Waterloo in 1815.

17:17.980 --> 17:21.500
Yes, it's the same "Waterloo" in this inn's name.

17:21.900 --> 17:29.220
I, as a sergeant of the Grand Army, fought alongside with Emperor
Napoleon in a valiant battle against our enemy, the Prussians.

17:29.830 --> 17:35.480
As a huge downpour from the other day had made the ground into
mud, even horses had slipped down but I continued my dash.

17:35.870 --> 17:37.850
Feast your eyes on this.

17:37.880 --> 17:49.910
Though we lost the battle, I risked my life there to save a certain
general who was shot while braving through a rain of bullets.

17:50.300 --> 17:53.910
This is the injury that I suffered during that time.

17:54.560 --> 17:56.790
Many thanks to the audience for listening.

18:04.360 --> 18:06.480
Black glass button?

18:06.740 --> 18:10.140
Yes. It seems like I have lost it...

18:10.700 --> 18:13.070
Is it a very valuable item?

18:13.080 --> 18:16.140
No, it isn't really valuable.

18:16.830 --> 18:21.690
But I bought it because it caught my interest.
So if you find it, can you send it to me?

18:22.590 --> 18:25.070
I'll leave some money here.

18:28.430 --> 18:30.280
If that's the case, we'll watch out for it.

18:32.470 --> 18:34.550
Well then, thank you for your consideration.

18:34.810 --> 18:35.540
See you.

18:37.890 --> 18:39.500
I'll go and search the rooms.

18:40.150 --> 18:42.380
You don't have to be concerned with this.

18:43.070 --> 18:45.670
Instead, you better go and start cleaning.

18:46.150 --> 18:50.760
Wash the clothes, fetch the water and clean
the floor. You need to do all of that!

18:51.990 --> 18:53.720
What's the matter, Éponine?

18:55.040 --> 18:57.180
Cosette stole it.

18:58.160 --> 18:59.390
What did you say?!

19:00.170 --> 19:03.610
Cosette stole that man's black glass button!

19:05.000 --> 19:06.690
Is this true, Cosette?!

19:07.260 --> 19:09.280
I didn't do it!

19:09.510 --> 19:11.610
You liar! I saw it!

19:11.640 --> 19:12.490
You liar!

19:12.510 --> 19:13.620
I didn't lie!

19:14.010 --> 19:17.580
You're really a bad girl to have stolen a customer's belongings.

19:18.020 --> 19:20.120
I didn't steal it!

19:20.560 --> 19:21.540
Come there, Cosette!

19:27.230 --> 19:30.010
Come clean or else...

19:35.490 --> 19:36.390
Hey! You stupid dog!

19:37.080 --> 19:39.180
Chou Chou! You can't go inside the house!

19:44.500 --> 19:47.770
Cosette, get that stupid dog out of here quickly!

19:49.380 --> 19:52.110
Chou Chou, you can't stay here! Be obedient and go outside!

20:05.400 --> 20:06.670
I found it!

20:10.440 --> 20:12.090
I'll go after them!

20:31.800 --> 20:32.990
What's wrong?

20:33.680 --> 20:34.530
Here.

20:34.550 --> 20:36.030
You found it?

20:36.050 --> 20:37.700
You dropped it in the bar.

20:38.260 --> 20:41.540
Thank you for coming all the way to return this to me.

20:44.100 --> 20:48.210
Um... What kind of a town is Montreuil-sur-Mer?

20:49.070 --> 20:52.980
It's a really lively, busy and a wonderful town.

20:53.490 --> 20:54.170
Why did you ask?

20:54.910 --> 20:56.800
My mother lives there.

20:57.120 --> 20:58.260
Really?

20:58.660 --> 21:05.020
Then, your mother and I might have passed
by each other somewhere in that town.

21:24.690 --> 21:25.620
Yes?

21:30.570 --> 21:31.960
Mademoiselle Zephyrine...

21:32.360 --> 21:35.170
I came here since I was nearby.

21:35.530 --> 21:38.890
Here you go.You forgot this.

21:39.160 --> 21:41.350
Thank you very much.

21:41.830 --> 21:43.470
Oh my. Are you writing a letter again?

21:43.500 --> 21:44.470
Y-Yes...

21:48.540 --> 21:49.810
I'll pour some tea.

22:03.560 --> 22:06.870
Cosette... Whose name is that?

22:13.390 --> 22:16.390
ma maman (my mother)

22:17.310 --> 22:20.560
I like you very much, Mother

22:17.310 --> 22:20.560
Daisukiyo nee okaasan

22:21.230 --> 22:24.610
I love you, Mother

22:21.230 --> 22:24.610
Aishiteru nee okaasan

22:25.230 --> 22:29.070
Your warm inviting scent

22:25.230 --> 22:29.070
Atataku ii nioi

22:29.070 --> 22:32.410
My precious mother

22:29.070 --> 22:32.410
Taisetsuna okaasan

22:33.240 --> 22:36.330
As long as you call out to me

22:33.240 --> 22:36.330
Yobikakeru sore dake de

22:37.290 --> 22:40.500
It brings me joy, Mother

22:37.290 --> 22:40.500
Ureshii no nee okaasan

22:41.210 --> 22:45.250
My only mother

22:41.210 --> 22:45.250
Kono sekai ni tatta hitori

22:45.250 --> 22:48.340
in this world

22:45.250 --> 22:48.340
Watashi no okaasan

22:49.680 --> 22:51.510
Hug me tightly

22:49.680 --> 22:51.510
Dakishimete gyutto

22:51.510 --> 22:53.470
Kiss me gently

22:51.510 --> 22:53.470
Kisu wo shitte sotto

22:53.470 --> 23:01.190
Always be by my side

22:53.470 --> 23:01.190
Itsudemo watashi no soba ni ite ne

23:01.690 --> 23:04.480
On the path lined with chestnut trees

23:01.690 --> 23:04.480
Maronie no michi

23:04.480 --> 23:09.450
we walk hand-in-hand

23:04.480 --> 23:09.450
Futari te wo tori aruku

23:09.450 --> 23:13.160
If we sing together,

23:09.450 --> 23:13.160
Isshoni utaeba

23:13.160 --> 23:17.330
we can have fun with just that.

23:13.160 --> 23:17.330
Tanoshii ne sore dake de

23:17.620 --> 23:21.540
Bathing in the sunlight filtering through the canopy

23:17.620 --> 23:21.540
Komorebi no naka yureru

23:21.540 --> 23:25.550
Your beautiful eyes

23:21.540 --> 23:25.550
Kirei na hitomi

23:25.550 --> 23:29.170
And that gentle smile

23:25.550 --> 23:29.170
Yawaraka na hohoemi de

23:29.170 --> 23:34.850
envelop me.

23:29.170 --> 23:34.850
Watashi wo tsutsumu no

23:39.560 --> 24:09.420
Preview

23:41.950 --> 23:45.260
Mayor Madeleine has such amazing strength.
He managed to save Monsieur Fauchelevent.

23:45.280 --> 23:48.140
But it caught Inspector Javert's attention. This is bad.

23:48.160 --> 23:48.930
This is bad.

23:48.950 --> 23:51.700
Let's change the topic. The village Cosette is in is called Montfermeil.

23:51.710 --> 23:54.560
The town Fantine and Madeleine are in is called Montreuil-sur-Mer.

23:54.590 --> 23:56.520
They look similar, but don't mix them up.

23:56.550 --> 24:01.070
Maybe because of this, Cosette got to know more about
the city her mother is in, so Cosette is happy.

24:01.090 --> 24:03.570
Next episode is: Cosette's Birthday.

24:03.590 --> 24:04.410
A birthday?

24:04.420 --> 24:09.420
Cosette's Birthday

24:04.430 --> 24:05.950
How old is Cosette?

24:05.970 --> 24:08.240
You better get along with her, Éponine.

24:24.480 --> 24:29.480
Look forward to the next Episode!
